Z||000000||Mickey_Moose||09-27-2001||06:05 PM||||Does this or any other Pontiac CD players have the red back lighting?<P>thanks<BR>Tim<BR> <A HREF="http://www.edmontonfieros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.edmontonfieros.com</A> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-27-2001||11:46 PM||||Any late model Pontiac CD radio will have red back lighting. The station/clock display will also be red. You will need the GM harness adapter to make it a plug and play on non sub systems. The lighting is a little brighter red than the the stock radio.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||09-28-2001||09:19 AM||||Not ANY late model pontiac....My friends 98 Firebird has a factory cd player with equ and it has orange lighting....<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-28-2001||11:29 AM||||I have the UP3. Love it! The lighting looks red to some, orange to others. I call it orange. <BR>The clock/frequency display on the UP3 is blue, like the factory radio. I think the later ones have the red (orange?) clock display.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
